sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Caller as Core API caller (tests or future frontend)
    participant Game as GameController
    participant State as GameState
    participant Content as ContentCatalog
    participant Grades as GradeBook
    participant Runner as JavaAssessmentRunner
    participant Save as SaveManager

    Note over Caller,Save: Implemented foundation, not complete gameplay. Fixture values are not approved rules.
    Caller->>Game: Construct with initial state, explicit RuleValues and ContentCatalog
    Note over Game,State: Every changing operation works on a copy and commits only after success.
    opt Opening not acknowledged
        Caller->>Game: completeOpening()
        Game->>State: Mark opening completed
        Note over Caller,Game: Actual opening battle/dialogue remains T01/T11, not rendered by this method.
    end
    alt Lesson slot
        Caller->>Game: showLesson()
        Game->>Content: lesson(day)
        Content-->>Game: Text, ask OR raise-hand interaction, configured choices
        Game->>State: Record content shown
        Game-->>Caller: Lesson content
        Caller->>Game: lessonChoice(choice)
        Game->>State: Apply supplied effects, waive tutorial penalties, advance to OTHER_CLASSES
        Note over Caller,Game: Exactly one choice because the successful operation consumes the class slot.
    else Assessment slot
        Caller->>Game: startAssessment()
        Game->>Content: questions(originalPlan, random)
        Content-->>Game: Fixed ordinary bank or configured major sample
        Game->>State: Open active assessment and apply configured makeup conditions if relevant
        Game-->>Caller: Questions, makeup flag, peeking and detection conditions
        opt Separate trusted local Java evaluation
            Caller->>Runner: evaluate(className, source, tests, rubric)
            Runner-->>Caller: Compilation, test outcomes and independent style findings
            Note over Caller,Runner: Evidence only. T06 decides how to assign a course mark.
        end
        opt Estimator supplied for an ordinary assessment
            Caller->>Game: recordSelfEstimate(mark, cost, provisionalSanDelta)
            Game->>State: Separate estimate, SAN cost and source-labelled provisional effect
            Note over Caller,Game: No invented accuracy model. Major-exam estimates/repeats report T08.
        end
        opt Cheating detected by a configured caller
            Caller->>Game: caughtCheating(serious)
            alt Tutorial
                Game-->>Caller: Warning only
            else Ordinary semester
                Game->>State: Configured SAN loss and serious-zero flag if applicable
            end
        end
        Caller->>Game: recordEvaluatedSubmission(mark, evidence)
        Note over Caller,Game: Evaluator output, not a player's answer or an HP conversion.
        Game->>Grades: Store submission, preserving any serious-cheating zero
        alt Ordinary Lab or Unit Test including makeup
            Grades-->>Game: Pending mark, return day = submission day + 3
            Game->>State: Advance to OTHER_CLASSES
        else Midterm or Final
            Grades-->>Game: Immediate official mark
            Game->>State: Enter MIDTERM_DECISION or FINAL_DECISION
            Note over Caller,State: No automatic continuation, Final combat or ending formula is claimed.
        end
    else Review slot
        Caller->>Game: completeReview()
        Game->>Content: review(day)
        Game->>State: Apply explicitly supplied review effect and finish class
    end

    opt Active run has reached OTHER_CLASSES
        Caller->>Game: otherClasses(reviseIcs)
        Game->>State: Focus = no stat change, revision = supplied +XP/-SAN effect
        Game->>State: Advance to AFTER_SCHOOL
        alt Sleep immediately after school
            Caller->>Game: sleepImmediatelyAfterSchool()
            Game->>State: Record morning half-slot and supplied SAN bonus, close day
        else Hub activities
            loop One accepted activity per named Hub period
                Caller->>Game: hubActivity(activityId)
                Game->>Content: hub(activityId)
                Game->>State: Apply configured effect and consume current slot
                opt Late night used outside tutorial
                    Game->>State: Record next-day SAN reduction and XP gain multiplier
                end
                Note over Game,State: Tutorial penalties only warn, never schedule a deferred penalty.
            end
        end
        Caller->>Save: saveAtDayEnd(game.snapshot(), path)
        Save->>Save: Validate, write temporary versioned file, atomically replace destination
        Save-->>Caller: Success or explicit failure
        Caller->>Save: load(path)
        Save-->>Caller: Same closed-day snapshot, no automatic time advancement
        Caller->>Game: Construct controller with restored state and compatible policy/content
        Caller->>Game: beginNextDay()
        Game->>State: Expire old effects, activate dated effects, grant earned morning entitlement once
        Game->>Grades: releaseDue(day)
        Grades-->>Game: Newly official ordinary results
        Game->>State: Remove only corresponding estimate values/effects
        Game-->>Caller: New day and explicit pending grade-feedback notice
        opt Earned morning half-slot
            Caller->>Game: hubActivity(activityId)
            Game->>State: Half numerical activity values, then enter ICS_CLASS
        end
    end

    opt Caller supplies approved official-grade feedback
        Caller->>Game: applyOfficialFeedback(assessmentId, effect)
        Game->>State: Apply once after official release, retaining unrelated effects
    end
    opt Midterm choice
        Caller->>Game: resolveMidterm(choice)
        alt Drop
            Game->>State: Mark run DROPPED
        else Continue or Retake
            Game-->>Caller: Explicit T10 pending-rule exception, state unchanged
        end
        Note over Game,State: Two-opportunity counter helper exists. Complete reset, low-SAN priority and ending saves remain TBD.
    end
    Note over Caller,Save: Invalid choices or missing rule/content inputs preserve state. No hidden game defaults or mid-activity saves.
